//! The `Syscalls` trait with one async method per syscall, the request enum, the `Layered` adapter,
//! user-memory reference types, result and restart types, and the return-to-guest interface.
//!
//! Everything above the kernel talks to it only through this crate. The trait, the request enum
//! and the adapter are generated by `wasixv2-codegen` from `lib/wasixv2/codegen/wit`; see the
//! header of `src/generated.rs`.
//!
//! On syscall returns and preemption points exec checks the task's WorkFlag once. When raised,
//! it awaits Control::run_task_work with the current Caller before draining take_pending's
//! signals/actions. This is the kernel's memory-bearing task_work_run boundary; a notification
//! wakes interruptible calls without fabricating a signal, using their normal restart policy.

mod caller;
mod control;
mod cputime;
mod generated;
